  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 101 PM MST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nSatellite imagery shows broad ridge folded over across Idaho early \nthis afternoon. Pockets of low clouds continue across the northern \nportions of the Snake Plain, and into the Divide and Island Park \nareas, while high cloud is trying to stream in from the northwest. \nThe ridge will continue to build, and the incoming upper moisture is \nexpected to have little impact with dry conditions forecast across \nthe region. Models feature a couple of weak shortwave features that \nhelp to flatten the ridge slightly, but recent runs have pulled any \npotential moisture further north, reducing the chance for showers to \nnear zero. Temperatures throughout much of the week remain above \nnormal. By next weekend, we are still seeing potential for the ridge \nto break down as moisture and energy work inland around a deep low \noff the Pacific coast. Ensemble means and the NBM continue to \nintroduce precipitation as early as Friday, but clusters still show \nquite a bit of variability. Confidence remains low for now.",
